BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kunstpunt-groningen-tschumi-pavilion-hellend-vlak-2027@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261104
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261105
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kunstpunt Groningen: Open Call Tschumi Pavilion (Hellend 
 Vlak 2027)
DESCRIPTION:Kunstpunt Groningen invites artists to propose a temporary\, si
 te-specific artwork for the Tschumi Pavilion on Hereplein\, Groningen\, vi
 ewable from outside\, that responds to current social and often polarised 
 issues. The brief asks how art can encourage us to look at today's social 
 issues in a different light. Prior experience with public space or commiss
 ions is not required\, and a previously unrealised concept may be submitte
 d. WHAT YOU GET: up to three shortlisted artists receive EUR 1\,500 (excl.
  VAT) each to develop a preliminary design\; the chosen artist realises th
 e work with a EUR 17\,000 budget including their fee. ELIGIBILITY: artists
  currently working in the city or province of Groningen\, or with a demons
 trable connection to it. APPLICATION: preferably one PDF with a one-page A
 4 cover letter in Dutch or English (why you should receive the commission 
 and what you want the public to experience)\, a CV covering 2022 to 2026\,
  and a website or social media link. DEADLINE: 4 November 2026 for stateme
 nts of intent. Shortlist announced 12 November 2026\, site visit the week 
 of 23 November\, preliminary designs and selection in the second week of J
 anuary 2027\, final design end of February\, opening June 2027 and dismant
 ling September 2027. Contact: nicolinewijnja@kunstpuntgroningen.nl (subjec
 t 'Open Call Hellend Vlak 2027').\n\nOrganisation: Kunstpunt Groningen\nLo
 cation: Tschumi Pavilion\, Hereplein\, Groningen\, Netherlands. Applicants
  must currently work in the city or province of Groningen or have a demons
 trable connection to it.\nAward: Up to three shortlisted artists receive E
 UR 1\,500 (excl. VAT) each for a preliminary design\; the selected artist 
 receives a EUR 17\,000 project budget\, including their fee. No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: Commission\; work on display 3 to 4 months (June to Sept
 ember 2027)\n\nMore: https://www.kunstpuntgroningen.nl/en/tschumi-pavilion
 /open-call-tschumi-pavilion/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://www.kunstpuntgroningen.nl/en/tschumi-pavilion/open-call-tschumi
 -pavilion/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Tschumi Pavilion\, Hereplein\, Groningen\, Netherlands. Applicants
  must currently work in the city or province of Groningen or have a demons
 trable connection to it.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ecf-erasmus-40-creative-research-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: European Cultural Foundation: ERASMUS 40 Creative Researc
 h Fellowship (Florence archives\, Brussels presentation)
DESCRIPTION:To mark the 40th anniversary of ERASMUS in 2027\, the European 
 Cultural Foundation is opening its historical archives for a Creative Rese
 arch Fellowship: one professional creative practitioner will research ECF'
 s lesser-known role in shaping the ERASMUS student mobility programme (fro
 m the European Institute of Education and the Office for Cooperation in Ed
 ucation to the ERASMUS Bureau\, which ran the scheme until 1994) and trans
 late that history into a public-facing artwork about what European belongi
 ng feels like and what the next ERASMUS could be. WHAT YOU GET: a EUR 10\,
 000 grant for travel\, living costs and production\; a research residency 
 at the Historical Archives of the European Union in Florence during the fi
 rst trimester of 2027\; and presentation of the finished work in Brussels 
 in September 2027\, in partnership with the House of European History. WHO
 : creative practitioners residing in a Council of Europe member state with
  a track record of research-based work for museum contexts. DEADLINE: 1 De
 cember 2026\, 17:00 CET. The full call is linked from ECF's open calls and
  social channels\; a dedicated call page could not be located at the time 
 of adding.\n\nOrganisation: European Cultural Foundation (ECF)\, with the 
 Historical Archives of the European Union (EUI) and the House of European 
 History\nLocation: Research stay in Florence\, Italy (Historical Archives 
 of the EU) in the first trimester of 2027\; final work presented in Brusse
 ls in September 2027. Open to creative practitioners residing in a Council
  of Europe member state.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 grant covering travel\, livin
 g expenses and artistic production. One fellowship.\nDuration: Research re
 sidency in Florence in the first trimester of 2027 (January to March)\; pr
 esentation in September 2027\n\nMore: https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-c
 alls/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Research stay in Florence\, Italy (Historical Archives of the EU) 
 in the first trimester of 2027\; final work presented in Brussels in Septe
 mber 2027. Open to creative practitioners residing in a Council of Europe 
 member state.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:netherland-america-foundation-cultural-grant-2026-11@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Netherland-America Foundation: Cultural Grant Program (1 
 November 2026 Cut-Off)
DESCRIPTION:The Netherland-America Foundation funds professional artistic a
 nd cultural projects that show a clear exchange between Dutch and American
  artists\, institutions or audiences\, such as exhibitions\, performances 
 and other cultural initiatives that promote dialogue and collaboration. Bo
 th emerging artists and established organisations may apply. NOT FUNDED: a
 pplicants who are not working cultural professionals\, seminar attendance\
 , degree tuition\, residencies\, research\, projects without a Dutch-Ameri
 can connection (these are not forwarded to the committee)\, and projects a
 lready underway or finished at the time of review. TIMING: apply at least 
 6 months before the money is needed\; a letter of intent is optional and e
 ncouraged for projects 9 or more months out\, after which the committee ma
 y invite a full application. Recent grantees must wait three years before 
 reapplying. Letter and budget in English\, addressed to the NAF Cultural C
 ommittee\; include visuals where relevant. QUARTERLY CUT-OFFS: 1 February 
 (window 2 Nov-1 Feb\, results mid-March)\, 1 May (results mid-June)\, 1 Au
 gust (results mid-September) and 1 November (window 2 Aug-1 Nov\, results 
 mid-December). Submit via Submittable.\n\nOrganisation: The Netherland-Ame
 rica Foundation (NAF)\nLocation: Netherlands and United States. For profes
 sional artists and cultural organisations running projects with a clear Du
 tch-American exchange.\nAward: Typically up to USD 5\,000 per project\, de
 pending on scope and impact\; higher amounts possible depending on availab
 le budget. No application fee.\n\nMore: https://thenaf.submittable.com/sub
 mit/208687/the-netherland-america-foundation-cultural-grant-program?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://thenaf.submittable.com/submit/208687/the-netherland-america-fou
 ndation-cultural-grant-program?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands and United States. For professional artists and cultur
 al organisations running projects with a clear Dutch-American exchange.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gainssa-ai-safety-essentials-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Deadline: GAIN SSA: AI Safety Essentials Fellowship (inaugural coho
 rt)
DESCRIPTION:GAIN SSA (Global AI Youth Network\, Sub-Saharan Africa) runs th
 e AI Safety Essentials Fellowship for residents of Africa considering how 
 they can be effective contributors in shaping the continent's transition t
 oward containing risks from transformative AI. Fellows spend six weeks map
 ping the priorities and gaps that need to be filled in Africa's AI safety 
 ecosystem\, through curated pre-reading and a live group call each week (a
 bout 5 hours per week). CURRICULUM: existential risks and catastrophic vec
 tors\; frontier AI models and Africa\; defining safe and beneficial AI\; s
 ubfields and alignment architectures\; Africa's AI safety landscape and po
 licy\; and a capstone week on fellowships and career launch\, with guidanc
 e toward international pipelines such as MATS\, ERA\, BlueDot and GovAI. M
 entorship comes from international AI safety researchers\, governance fell
 ows and peer builders. FUNDING: after the program\, top capstone action-pl
 an proposals are funded from a USD 500 to 1\,000 micro-grant pool (capped 
 at USD 1\,000)\, including proposals needing compute\, travel to AI alignm
 ent conferences in Sub-Saharan Africa\, or communication work (for example
  Substack Pro for writers)\; results are shared within 10 days of receivin
 g a proposal. The main aim is to have participants take action to build Af
 rica's first AI safety systems. APPLICATION: expression of interest for th
 e inaugural cohort via the Google Form linked from the program page. DEADL
 INE: expressions of interest close 8 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: GAIN 
 SSA (Global AI Youth Network\, Sub-Saharan Africa)\nLocation: Online (virt
 ual\, facilitated). Open to residents of African countries.\nAward: Micro-
 grant pool funding top capstone proposals at USD 500 to 1\,000 each (cappe
 d at USD 1\,000)\, usable for compute access\, communication work such as 
 Substack Pro subscriptions for writers\, or travel to AI alignment confere
 nces in Sub-Saharan Africa. The fellowship itself is free to attend (no pa
 rticipation fee\, no application fee)\; no stipend is paid during the prog
 ram.\nDuration: 6-week facilitated virtual curriculum plus an onboarding p
 re-requisites module (the site also describes it as 7 weeks)\, about 5 hou
 rs per week with one live group call per week\; capstone proposals are fun
 ded afterwards\, with results within 10 days of submission.\n\nMore: https
 ://gainssa.org/initiatives/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://gainssa.org/initiatives/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (virtual\, facilitated). Open to residents of African count
 ries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a4-residency-chengdu-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Fellowsh
 ip 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:The A4 Residency Art Center in Chengdu\, the residency platform
  of the A4 Art Museum in Luxelakes Eco-City\, opens its full-year 2028 rec
 ruitment. The interdisciplinary\, open and collaborative platform fosters 
 creative exchange among artists\, scientists\, writers and other professio
 nals\, with residents initiating participatory local activities that conne
 ct them with the city and community\; A4 also organises group activities\,
  sharing sessions\, media promotion and exhibition opportunities. CYCLES: 
 Spring 2028 (April to June) and Autumn 2028 (July to October)\, each appro
 ximately eight weeks. WHAT YOU GET (International Residency Fellowship\, f
 ully funded): private studio and accommodation\, round-trip economy airfar
 e or second-class train within a set budget\, a production grant of RMB 10
 \,000 per person or team for materials and production (excluding living ex
 penses)\, community engagement and cultural experiences\, media promotion 
 and networking. ELIGIBILITY: multidisciplinary creators worldwide\, includ
 ing visual and performing artists\, musicians\, filmmakers\, architects\, 
 curators\, designers and creatives with interdisciplinary backgrounds brid
 ging art\, business and culture. APPLICATION: free\; submit a photo\, port
 folio\, CV and project proposal in English and Chinese to a4residency@a4am
 .cn\, with the subject line specifying the programme tier and preferred cy
 cle. DEADLINE: 31 December 2026 for the 2028 full-year recruitment. A para
 llel self-funded light track exists\; this listing covers the funded fello
 wship only.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center (A4 Art Museum)\nLoca
 tion: Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open worldwi
 de.\nAward: Fully funded fellowship: private studio and accommodation\, ro
 und-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket within a set budget\
 , and a production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for materials and 
 production (excluding living expenses). No application fee.\nDuration: App
 roximately 8 weeks\, in the Spring 2028 (April to June) or Autumn 2028 (Ju
 ly to October) cycle.\n\nMore: https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residency
 artcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open world
 wide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:graner-creative-grants-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:Deadline: Graner Creative Grants 2027: Residencies for Dance and Li
 ve Arts (Barcelona)
DESCRIPTION:Graner\, Barcelona's centre for dance and live arts creation wi
 thin the city council's Creative Factories Network\, managed by Mercat de 
 les Flors with the Catalan dance professionals' associations APDC and ACPD
 C\, opens its 2027 call for residency grants supporting creation and resea
 rch projects taking place between January and December 2027. EIGHT CATEGOR
 IES: Associated Artist (1 place\, EUR 6\,000 per year for 2027 and 2028\, 
 for Catalonia-based artists who associate with the centre for two years\, 
 with a creative residency of up to six weeks)\; Creation (3 places\, EUR 6
 \,000\, local and national artists developing projects leading to a produc
 tion\, up to five weeks)\; Barcelona Crea Research (2 places\, EUR 6\,000\
 , local researchers and artists in the initial stages of artistic research
  with body\, movement and choreographic thinking as its axes)\; Barcelona 
 Crea Critical Thinking (1 place\, EUR 6\,000\, theoretical\, critical or d
 iscursive projects on dance and the live arts)\; International (1 place\, 
 EUR 3\,000\, for researchers\, artists and collectives based outside Spain
  without a direct connection to the Catalan or Spanish context\, two to fo
 ur weeks\; applying here excludes all other categories)\; Stage Research (
 1 place\, EUR 3\,000\, research centred on lighting\, sound\, video or sce
 nography\, with technical studio time and support sessions)\; Emerging Art
 ists (2 places\, EUR 3\,000\, endowment topped up with EUR 1\,700 contribu
 ted by Can Gassol in Mataro\, where part of the residency takes place)\; a
 nd Practical Methodologies (1 place\, EUR 3\,000). WHAT YOU GET: on top of
  the grant\, a workspace agreed per project\, possible technical residency
 \, shared desk and facilities\, artistic support and possible specialised 
 mentoring\, participation in Graner's labs\, workshops and seminars\, comm
 unication support\, and covered national and European travel to the two an
 nual APLEC gatherings. ELIGIBILITY: natural persons\, legal persons and gr
 oups with or without legal personality\; applicants may apply to at most t
 wo categories (International is mutually exclusive) and can receive only o
 ne grant. Barcelona Crea categories require a demonstrated connection to B
 arcelona or its metropolitan area and carry municipal-grant incompatibilit
 y rules. NOTE: structural renovation works run at Graner throughout 2027 a
 nd may affect studio use. APPLICATION: free\, via the category-specific fo
 rms on the Mercat de les Flors website\; an English-language bases PDF det
 ails each category. DEADLINE: 29 September 2026 at 14:00 Catalan time (12:
 00 UTC).\n\nOrganisation: El Graner Fabrica de Creacio\, managed by Mercat
  de les Flors\nLocation: Graner\, Barcelona\, Spain (with part of the Emer
 ging Artists residencies at Can Gassol\, Mataro). Most categories are for 
 local and national artists\; one International category is reserved for ar
 tists based outside Spain.\nAward: 12 grants totalling EUR 57\,000. EUR 6\
 ,000 per project for Associated Artist (1 place\, EUR 6\,000 each for 2027
  and 2028)\, Creation (3 places)\, Barcelona Crea Research (2) and Barcelo
 na Crea Critical Thinking (1). EUR 3\,000 per project for Stage Research (
 1)\, International (1)\, Emerging Artists (2\, endowment topped up with EU
 R 1\,700 from Can Gassol) and Practical Methodologies (1). Plus workspace\
 , possible technical residency\, artistic support and covered travel to th
 e two annual APLEC gatherings. No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies 
 between January and December 2027\, typically up to four to six weeks\, no
 t necessarily consecutive\, depending on category. The Associated Artist c
 ommits for two years (2027-2028).\n\nMore: https://mercatflors.cat/en/beca
 /2027-call-for-proposals-for-creative-grants-el-graner-fabrica-de-creacio/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://mercatflors.cat/en/beca/2027-call-for-proposals-for-creative-gr
 ants-el-graner-fabrica-de-creacio/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Graner\, Barcelona\, Spain (with part of the Emerging Artists resi
 dencies at Can Gassol\, Mataro). Most categories are for local and nationa
 l artists\; one International category is reserved for artists based outsi
 de Spain.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:supporting-act-foundation-artist-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Supporting Act Foundation: Artist Grant 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Supporting Act Foundation\, the charitable foundation estab
 lished by WeTransfer\, awards ten unrestricted Artist Grants of EUR 10\,00
 0 to emerging artists from underrepresented groups whose work involves col
 laborative\, collective or creative processes that benefit their communiti
 es. The grant is paid as EUR 1\,000 per month over one year and can be use
 d freely\; applicants should explain how it would help them overcome econo
 mic\, social\, cultural\, physical or health barriers to their practice. E
 LIGIBILITY: identify as an emerging artist with at least two and no more t
 han ten years of professional experience\; identify as belonging to an und
 errepresented group or face systemic barriers to your career\; be born in 
 or before 2005\; be based in Belgium\, France\, Germany\, Greece\, Ireland
 \, Italy\, the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain or the United Kingdom with a
  personal IBAN bank account there\; and have an updated website or public 
 social media profile. Former and current TSAF grantees cannot apply. TIMEL
 INE: applications close 1 October 2026 at 11:00 CET\, notifications go to 
 all applicants in late October 2026\, shortlisted applicants get a final r
 eview in November 2026\, and the public announcement and first transfer fo
 llow in January 2027. APPLICATION: free\, via the open call platform on th
 e foundation's website. The parallel Impact Grant strand for arts nonprofi
 ts runs on the same deadline.\n\nOrganisation: The Supporting Act Foundati
 on\nLocation: Remote\; for artists based in Belgium\, France\, Germany\, G
 reece\, Ireland\, Italy\, the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain or the United
  Kingdom.\nAward: 10 unrestricted grants of EUR 10\,000 each\, paid out at
  EUR 1\,000 per month over one year\, with the first installment transferr
 ed in January 2027. No application fee.\nDuration: One year\, from January
  2027.\n\nMore: https://thesupportingact.org/programs/artist-grant/2026?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://thesupportingact.org/programs/artist-grant/2026?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\; for artists based in Belgium\, France\, Germany\, Greece\
 , Ireland\, Italy\, the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain or the United Kingd
 om.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:supporting-act-foundation-impact-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Supporting Act Foundation: Impact Grant 2026 for Arts
  Nonprofits
DESCRIPTION:The Supporting Act Foundation\, the charitable foundation estab
 lished by WeTransfer\, awards ten unrestricted Impact Grants of EUR 50\,00
 0 (EUR 25\,000 per year over two years) to arts-focused nonprofits that em
 power emerging artists from underrepresented groups through non-financial 
 support: improving artists' living conditions\, enabling practice developm
 ent\, increasing the visibility of their work and building their confidenc
 e. ELIGIBILITY: nonprofits registered as arts organizations between 2016 a
 nd 2024\, based in Belgium\, France\, Germany\, Greece\, Ireland\, Italy\,
  the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain or the United Kingdom\, or working wit
 h a fiscal host in one of these countries\; annual expenditures between EU
 R 50\,000 and EUR 300\,000\; an active website demonstrating supported pro
 jects\; and an IBAN bank account. Individuals\, commercial entities\, curr
 ent or past TSAF grantees\, and proposals for ongoing projects rather than
  established organizations are not eligible. TIMELINE: applications close 
 1 October 2026 at 11:00 CET\, are reviewed in October\, notifications go o
 ut in late October 2026\, shortlisted organizations get a final review in 
 November 2026\, and the public announcement and first installment follow i
 n January 2027. APPLICATION: free\, via the open call platform on the foun
 dation's website. The parallel Artist Grant strand for individual emerging
  artists runs on the same deadline.\n\nOrganisation: The Supporting Act Fo
 undation\nLocation: Remote\; for nonprofits registered in Belgium\, France
 \, Germany\, Greece\, Ireland\, Italy\, the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain
  or the United Kingdom\, or working with a fiscal host there.\nAward: 10 u
 nrestricted grants of EUR 50\,000 each\, paid as EUR 25\,000 per year over
  two years\, with the first transfer in January 2027. No application fee.\
 nDuration: Two years\, from January 2027.\n\nMore: https://thesupportingac
 t.org/programs/impact-grant/2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://thesupportingact.org/programs/impact-grant/2026?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\; for nonprofits registered in Belgium\, France\, Germany\,
  Greece\, Ireland\, Italy\, the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain or the Unit
 ed Kingdom\, or working with a fiscal host there.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pedantic-arts-residency-and-research-grant-2027@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pedantic Arts Residency and Research Grant 2027 (Pittsbur
 gh)
DESCRIPTION:Pedantic Arts Residency opens applications for its Summer 2027 
 and Fall 2027 programmes in Pittsburgh: two four-week residency cohorts an
 d two research grants. THE RESIDENCY houses three creatives at a time (a v
 isual artist\, an organizer and a writer) in a collective four-week progra
 mme that emphasizes exploration\, exchange and community connection over p
 roduction. Residents get free furnished housing in a shared apartment\, a 
 USD 2\,000 stipend to cover living expenses (half on arrival\, half on com
 pletion)\, a Pittsburgh-based guide working in their field\, tickets and i
 nstitutional passes\, and introductions across the city's creative communi
 ty. THE RESEARCH GRANT invites an individual visual artist\, curator or wr
 iter for a one- to two-week independent stay to conduct Pittsburgh-related
  research\, with a free private bedroom at the Pedantic Apartment\, a USD 
 500 or USD 1\,000 honorarium usable at the grantee's discretion\, and help
  establishing relevant connections. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must be 18 or 
 older and not Pittsburgh residents at the time of application\; travel cos
 ts are the participant's own. Residency attendance and staying in the prov
 ided housing are required. APPLICATION: applications are free until 28 Sep
 tember 2026 at 23:59 EST\; a USD 20 fee applies from then until the final 
 deadline of 15 October 2026 at 23:59 EST.\n\nOrganisation: Pedantic Arts R
 esidency\nLocation: Pittsburgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA. Open to non-Pittsburg
 h residents aged 18 or older\; travel is self-funded.\nAward: Residency: f
 ree furnished housing in a shared apartment plus a USD 2\,000 living stipe
 nd (half on arrival\, half on completion). Research Grant: a free private 
 bedroom at the Pedantic Apartment plus a USD 500 or USD 1\,000 honorarium 
 at the grantee's discretion. Application free until 28 September 2026\, th
 en USD 20.\nDuration: Residency: four weeks\, Summer 2027 or Fall 2027 coh
 orts. Research Grant: one to two weeks.\n\nMore: https://pedanticarts.org/
 announcements/open-call-for-residents-and-grantees-submit-by-october-15th/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://pedanticarts.org/announcements/open-call-for-residents-and-gran
 tees-submit-by-october-15th/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Pittsburgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA. Open to non-Pittsburgh residents 
 aged 18 or older\; travel is self-funded.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nordic-culture-fund-enter-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nordic Culture Fund: ENTER 2026 (exploratory cross-border
  collaboration)
DESCRIPTION:ENTER is the first programme in the Nordic Culture Fund's new p
 ortfolio\, designed to support ambitious ideas that need collaboration to 
 be explored and tested in practice. It offers space to experiment\, learn 
 as you go and test new directions through encounters across disciplines an
 d perspectives\, rather than funding finished productions. WHO CAN APPLY: 
 individuals\, groups\, organisations\, institutions\, associations and com
 panies\, from arts and culture or other sectors\, as long as arts and cult
 ure are central to the initiative. Initiatives need clear Nordic anchoring
  (interpreted flexibly) and cross-border collaboration\; applicants and pa
 rtners may be based anywhere\, and multiple applications for different ini
 tiatives are permitted. FUNDING: up to DKK 50\,000\, plus up to DKK 25\,00
 0 in accessibility support\, with no co-funding requirement. WHAT IT DOES 
 NOT SUPPORT: education or study visits\, conference or festival participat
 ion\, tours or travelling exhibitions\, productions or publications\, orga
 nisational running costs\, or construction and equipment purchases. APPLIC
 ATION: submitted electronically through the Fund's portal in Danish\, Norw
 egian\, Swedish\, Finnish or English\; no attachments are allowed\, so eve
 rything must fit in the form. Decisions come within five weeks of the dead
 line. The autumn 2026 window runs 14 September to 16 October 2026.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Nordic Culture Fund\nLocation: Nordic region and beyond. Initiat
 ives must have clear Nordic anchoring (interpreted flexibly) and cross-bor
 der collaboration\, but applicants and partners may be based anywhere.\nAw
 ard: Up to DKK 50\,000 (roughly EUR 6\,700)\, plus up to DKK 25\,000 in ad
 ditional accessibility support for logistics and access needs\, for a maxi
 mum total of DKK 75\,000. No co-funding required. No application fee.\nDur
 ation: Projects may run up to one year from the stated start date\, genera
 lly non-extendable.\n\nMore: https://nordiskkulturfond.org/en/funding-prog
 rammes/give-ambitious-ideas-space-to-grow-with-enter?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nordiskkulturfond.org/en/funding-programmes/give-ambitious-idea
 s-space-to-grow-with-enter?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:Nordic region and beyond. Initiatives must have clear Nordic ancho
 ring (interpreted flexibly) and cross-border collaboration\, but applicant
