BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:peripheral-acts-edition-2-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Deadline: Peripheral Acts Edition 2: Leaning Out (UAE balcony resid
 ency)
DESCRIPTION:Peripheral Acts is an experimental\, artist-led residency progr
 amme supporting artistic production alongside dialogue\, exchange and site
 -responsive experimentation\, rooted in everyday urban life in the UAE. Th
 e second edition\, Leaning Out\, takes residential balconies as its site: 
 suspended between private life and public view\, the balcony becomes a sta
 ge for negotiations between host and guest\, inhabitant and observer\, fra
 ming questions of privacy\, voyeurism\, belonging and ownership. STRUCTURE
 : three commissioned artists take part in two phases. Phase 1 is four in-p
 erson gatherings hosted by residency programmer Shazia Salam in Dubai and 
 Abu Dhabi (1\, 7\, 14 and 21 November 2026\, roughly two hours each\; atte
 ndance at all four is expected). Phase 2 is a one-month balcony takeover p
 er artist (January\, February or March 2027)\, during which each resident 
 also hosts one (semi-)public event sharing their practice and process. The
 re is no fixed formula for what can happen on the site\; interventions are
  shaped by its conditions\, permissions and chance encounters\, carefully 
 testing the possibilities and boundaries of informal public intervention i
 n the UAE. FUNDING: AED 1\,000 commission fee plus AED 1\,500 production b
 udget per artist. ELIGIBILITY: artists currently based in the UAE with eas
 y\, ongoing access to a residential balcony (their own or one belonging to
  a friend or family member). Questions: shaziasalam.92@gmail.com. APPLY vi
 a the Google Form. DEADLINE: 4 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Peripheral A
 cts\, conceptualised and hosted by Shazia Salam and Priyanka Mehra\nLocati
 on: Dubai and Abu Dhabi\, UAE. Open to artists currently based in the UAE 
 with easy\, ongoing access to a residential balcony (their own\, or a frie
 nd's or family member's).\nAward: AED 1\,000 artist commission fee plus AE
 D 1\,500 production budget per artist. Three artists commissioned. No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: Phase 1: four in-person gatherings in Dubai and Ab
 u Dhabi on 1\, 7\, 14 and 21 November 2026 (approx. 2 hours each). Phase 2
 : one-month balcony takeovers\, January\, February or March 2027 (one arti
 st per month).\n\nMore: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScVzoHsSO
 bapDUhXkeK02Ya1JpxzQH3QjVRtvhfoWDM-KWeSA/viewform?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScVzoHsSObapDUhXkeK02Ya1JpxzQH
 3QjVRtvhfoWDM-KWeSA/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Dubai and Abu Dhabi\, UAE. Open to artists currently based in the 
 UAE with easy\, ongoing access to a residential balcony (their own\, or a 
 friend's or family member's).
END:VEVENT
