UID:cultural-horizons-residencies-subgrants-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Cultural Horizons Residencies: Subgrants for EU Organisat
 ions Hosting Ukrainian Artists
DESCRIPTION:Cultural Horizons strengthens the cultural sector in Ukraine by
  promoting joint EU-Ukrainian cultural initiatives and expanding access fo
 r Ukrainians affected by the war to European cultural and artistic network
 s. The Residencies strand provides subgrants for EU-based institutions to 
 implement (a) residency placements and/or (b) education projects organised
  on the basis of residencies\, for and with Ukrainian artistic and cultura
 l professionals in 2027. WHO CAN APPLY: artistic and cultural organisation
 s and initiatives registered within the EU\; consortia designate one lead 
 organisation to submit and manage funding. Applicants must demonstrate the
  ability to host Ukrainian artistic and cultural professionals in 2027 and
  complete projects between January and August 2027\, confirm the absence o
 f ties with the Russian Federation (no working partnerships with Russia or
  Russian organisations\, no visits to Russian-occupied territories after 2
 014)\, commit to refraining from glorification of Russian imperialism\, co
 mply with the EU sanctions regime\, and demonstrate a commitment to divers
 ity\, equity and inclusion. NGOs and public sector institutions working wi
 th displaced and vulnerable groups are prioritised. WHO IT SUPPORTS: Ukrai
 nian artists and cultural practitioners (independent and employed professi
 onals\, early-career specialists\, debut artists\, cultural managers\, res
 earchers\, analysts\, conservators)\, vulnerable groups from Ukraine inclu
 ding internally displaced persons\, young artists and communities in front
 line and conflict-affected areas\, and Ukrainian cultural organisations wi
 th a focus on small communities\, local initiatives\, independent cultural
  spaces and NGOs. TIMELINE: applications 29 June to 30 September 2026\; ev
 aluation October to November 2026\; implementation 1 January to 30 July 20
 27. The programme runs 2026-2027 and also builds a Europe-wide network of 
 cultural expert mentors. Queries: culturalhorizons[at]culturalvistas.eu.\n
 \nOrganisation: Ukrainian Cultural Foundation and Cultural Vistas\, funded
  by the Creative Europe Programme of the European Union\nLocation: Europea
 n Union. Open to artistic and cultural organisations and initiatives regis
 tered within the EU\; residency and education projects host Ukrainian arti
 stic and cultural professionals during 2027.\nAward: Subgrants of EUR 5\,0
 00 to 20\,000 each\; a minimum of 20 subgrants will be awarded. No applica
 tion fee.\nDuration: Projects run 1 January to 30 July 2027\, minimum 3 an
 d maximum 8 months\; final reports due within one month of completion and 
 no later than 15 August 2027\n\nMore: https://culturalvistas.eu/our-progra
 ms/professional-study-tours/cultural-horizons?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral#residencies
URL:https://culturalvistas.eu/our-programs/professional-study-tours/cultura
 l-horizons?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral#resid
 encies
LOCATION:European Union. Open to artistic and cultural organisations and in
 itiatives registered within the EU\; residency and education projects host
  Ukrainian artistic and cultural professionals during 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ses12naus-two-phase-residency-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fundacion Ses12naus: Two-Phase Residency for Visual Artis
 ts and Curators\, Ibiza (2026-2027)
DESCRIPTION:Ses12naus\, a non-profit founded in 2016 to strengthen the cult
 ural and artistic fabric of Ibiza and develop the island as an internation
 al reference for contemporary artistic creation\, is launching a two-phase
  residency for visual artists and curators at any career stage. Four proje
 cts are selected for the 2026-2027 edition: two by artists or curators bas
 ed in the Balearic Islands\, one from the rest of Spain and one from anoth
 er European country. STRUCTURE: Phase 1 (21 November to 13 December 2026) 
 is dedicated to research and exploration of the territory and an in-depth 
 understanding of the local context\, with a required public activity linke
 d to the process\; between phases the Foundation's team actively follows u
 p on the conceptualisation and formalisation of the proposal\; in Phase 2 
 (17 May to 7 June 2027) residents return to produce and present: artists p
 roduce their works\, curators continue their research\, and both present r
 esults. The format supports developing a new project or giving continuity 
 to an ongoing one\, in dialogue with Ibiza and its communities. FUNDING: E
 UR 1\,800 honorarium plus EUR 300 public-activity fee per resident\; trave
 l up to EUR 330 (Spain) or EUR 770 (Europe) booked by the Foundation (no t
 ravel between phases is financed)\; production up to EUR 3\,000 for artist
 s plus EUR 500 installation and EUR 200 public-activity costs (curators: E
 UR 500 plus EUR 200). RESOURCES: private bedroom and bathroom with shared 
 kitchen and living room\, a workspace at La Carpinteria sized to the proje
 ct with projectors\, speakers\, machinery and tools (specific materials no
 t in the inventory come from the production budget)\, production assistanc
 e\, a shared car for the duration (valid driving licence required) and air
 port transfers. APPLICATION: online form\, deadline 30 September 2026\, 23
 :59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: Fundacion Ses12naus\nLocation: Ibiza\, Balearic 
 Islands\, Spain (at La Carpinteria creation centre\, Can Bufi). Open to vi
 sual artists and curators residing in the Balearic Islands\, Spain and Eur
 ope: of four selected projects\, two go to the Balearic Islands\, one to t
 he rest of Spain and one to another European country. No age limit.\nAward
 : Honorarium of EUR 1\,800 per resident (EUR 900 per phase) plus EUR 300 f
 or the public activity (all subject to taxes and withholdings). Travel up 
 to EUR 330 for participants from Spain or EUR 770 from other European coun
 tries (booked by the Foundation). Production: artists up to EUR 3\,000 for
  production and public presentation (including transport of the work)\, pl
 us up to EUR 500 installation costs and EUR 200 for public activities\; cu
 rators up to EUR 500 for the final presentation and EUR 200 for the public
  activity. Also included: private bedroom with private bathroom\, shared k
 itchen and living room\, workspace at La Carpinteria with technical resour
 ces\, production assistance\, a shared car (driving licence required) and 
 airport transfers. Free to apply.\nDuration: Two 3-week phases: 21 Novembe
 r to 13 December 2026 (research and territory exploration\, with a public 
 activity) and 17 May to 7 June 2027 (production and presentation)\, with a
 ctive follow-up between phases\n\nMore: https://ses12naus.org/en/applicati
 on-form-open-call-2026-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://ses12naus.org/en/application-form-open-call-2026-2027/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ibiza\, Balearic Islands\, Spain (at La Carpinteria creation centr
 e\, Can Bufi). Open to visual artists and curators residing in the Baleari
 c Islands\, Spain and Europe: of four selected projects\, two go to the Ba
 learic Islands\, one to the rest of Spain and one to another European coun
 try. No age limit.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-seed-grant-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Seed Grant\, Autumn 2026 round
DESCRIPTION:The Stokroos Seed Grant supports early-practice visual artists\
 , designers and craft practitioners in the Netherlands with an unrestricte
 d budget for a self-defined plan: EUR 5\,000 for individuals\, EUR 7\,500 
 for duos\, EUR 10\,000 for collectives. The plan must start at least 10 we
 eks after submission\, last no longer than a year\, and can take place any
 where in the world. WHO IS ELIGIBLE: makers who between 2018 and 2022 comp
 leted their first subject-specific HBO or MBO programme\, or started their
  practice without formal training (first public presentation or commission
  marks the start)\; at least 21 years old\; living and working in the King
 dom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at 
 least one year\; not enrolled in a study or post-academic programme during
  the grant period. RESTRICTIONS: one application per person every two cale
 ndar years\, a lifetime maximum of two Seed Grants\, and only one applicat
 ion per year across all Stokroos schemes. DEADLINE: the autumn window runs
  1 September to 31 October 2026\, but the form CLOSES EARLY once 60 eligib
 le applications are received\, so apply as soon as possible. TO APPLY: onl
 ine form (Dutch or English) with portfolio PDF (max 20 pages\, 10MB)\, CV\
 , work and plan descriptions and a timeline\; response within about 8 week
 s. Recipients acknowledge Stokroos in communication about the plan.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLocation: Applicants must live and work in 
 the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean parts) or Suriname
  for at least one year\; the funded plan itself can take place anywhere in
  the world.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 for individuals\, EUR 7\,500 for duos\, EUR
  10\,000 for collectives\, as an unrestricted contribution to a self-defin
 ed plan. No application fee.\nDuration: Funded plan starts at least 10 wee
 ks after submission and lasts up to one year\n\nMore: https://stokroos.nl/
 en/grant-rules/seed-en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/seed-en/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicants must live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (i
 ncluding its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; the fund
 ed plan itself can take place anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:perform-europe-open-call-2026-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
SUMMARY:Deadline: Perform Europe: Open Call 2026-2028 (cross-border touring
 )
DESCRIPTION:Perform Europe is the EU support scheme for cross-border tourin
 g and distribution of performing arts works across Creative Europe countri
 es. WHAT IT FUNDS: touring of completed performing arts works (all perform
 ing arts disciplines except live music and opera)\; it does NOT cover prod
 uction costs for new creations. Each proposal must present at least one ar
 tistic work in at least three different Creative Europe countries. GRANTS:
  EUR 15\,000\, EUR 25\,000 or EUR 55\,000 depending on project size\, with
  top-ups of up to EUR 5\,000 per proposal for sustainability and accessibi
 lity measures (maximum EUR 60\,000 total). WHO IS ELIGIBLE: partnerships o
 f at least three partners from at least three Creative Europe countries (t
 he 27 EU member states plus 14 non-EU participating countries)\; organizat
 ions and professionals in the performing arts sector. DEADLINE: 22 October
  2026\, 23:59 CEST. TO APPLY: via the Perform Europe platform linked from 
 the call page. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisation: Perform Europe (co-funded b
 y Creative Europe\, European Union)\nLocation: Creative Europe countries (
 27 EU member states plus 14 non-EU participating countries). Each partners
 hip needs at least three partners from at least three Creative Europe coun
 tries.\nAward: Three grant tiers: EUR 15\,000 (small)\, EUR 25\,000 (mediu
 m) or EUR 55\,000 (large) per proposal\, plus top-ups of up to EUR 5\,000 
 for sustainability and accessibility needs\; absolute maximum EUR 60\,000 
 per proposal including top-ups. No application fee.\nDuration: Touring pro
 jects within the 2026-2028 Perform Europe cycle\n\nMore: https://culture.e
 c.europa.eu/funding/calls/open-call-of-perform-europe-2026-2028?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culture.ec.europa.eu/funding/calls/open-call-of-perform-europe-
 2026-2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Creative Europe countries (27 EU member states plus 14 non-EU part
 icipating countries). Each partnership needs at least three partners from 
 at least three Creative Europe countries.
END:VEVENT
