UID:dcc-ballyfermot-library-visual-arts-commission-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Dublin City Council: Visual Arts Exhibition Commission fo
 r Ballyfermot Library (curated by IMMA)
DESCRIPTION:Dublin City Council's Creative Hubs programme\, delivered by Th
 e Ark and curated by IMMA (Irish Museum of Modern Art)\, invites submissio
 ns for its 5th Visual Arts Exhibition Commission: an exhibition created fo
 r children\, schools and families\, located in Ballyfermot Library for app
 roximately 10 weeks from April to June 2027. Proposals should respond to a
  general theme of nature and the natural world\, in line with IMMA's ongoi
 ng programme on climate\, culture and collective action (Earth Rising). Th
 e commissioned exhibition must give children under 12 a quality visual art
 s experience\, engage with the library setting and the Ballyfermot context
 \, and include opportunities for children to experience the artist's proce
 ss (a studio visit or field trip plus an audio or video interview by child
 ren before the exhibition opens)\; the artist also contributes to an educa
 tion and learning programme led by IMMA. Previous commissions in the serie
 s went to Aideen Barry (2015)\, Barbara Knezevic (2019)\, Jane Locke (2022
 ) and Lucy McKenna (2024). WHAT YOU GET: EUR 10\,000 for research and deli
 very of the commissioned works\, technical installation support from IMMA\
 , mentorship from the Arts Office if requested\, and an associated educati
 on programme run by IMMA across the exhibition's run. APPLICATION: a short
  proposal\, a brief history of your work and the principles of your practi
 ce\, and a broad outline of your idea for an accessible and engaging visua
 l arts exhibition for children\; submitted via the Dublin City Arts Office
  Submittable page. Assessment: quality visual arts experience for children
  30 percent\, engagement with the library context 20 percent\, cognisance 
 of the target age group and input on the engagement programme 30 percent\,
  feasibility and R&D structure 20 percent. A maximum of five proposals are
  shortlisted\; shortlisted artists meet representatives of the Arts Office
 \, Dublin City Libraries\, The Ark and IMMA on 29 October 2026\, with the 
 award notified in the week of 2 November 2026. DEADLINE: 15 October 2026\,
  12 noon.\n\nOrganisation: Dublin City Council Creative Hubs programme\, d
 elivered by The Ark\, curated by IMMA (Irish Museum of Modern Art)\nLocati
 on: Ballyfermot Library\, Dublin\, Ireland. The call does not state a resi
 dency or nationality restriction\; shortlisted artists meet the panel on 2
 9 October 2026 and the commission involves in-person engagement with child
 ren in Dublin (a studio visit or field trip and an interview by children).
 \nAward: EUR 10\,000 commission award for research and delivery of commiss
 ioned works for the exhibition. Technical support for installation is prov
 ided by IMMA\, and the artist is supported by Arts Office and Library staf
 f during the research phase. No application fee.\nDuration: Exhibition run
 s approximately 10 weeks\, April to June 2027\, in the exhibition room of 
 Ballyfermot Library\n\nMore: https://dublincityartsoffice.submittable.com/
 submit?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://dublincityartsoffice.submittable.com/submit?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ballyfermot Library\, Dublin\, Ireland. The call does not state a 
 residency or nationality restriction\; shortlisted artists meet the panel 
 on 29 October 2026 and the commission involves in-person engagement with c
 hildren in Dublin (a studio visit or field trip and an interview by childr
 en).
END:VEVENT
