DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Elephant Trust: Autumn 2026 Grant Round (UK)
DESCRIPTION:The Elephant Trust\, founded by Roland Penrose and Lee Miller\,
  funds experimental visual art in the UK and is one of the few no-fee UK f
 unds for individual artists with a live deadline this autumn\; the round o
 pened 18 September 2026. It funds making new work and realising exhibition
 s and is historically sympathetic to experimental and unconventional proje
 cts\, so media and installation work is fundable even though the Trust is 
 an art fund rather than an art-tech institution. WHAT YOU GET: grants of u
 p to GBP 5\,000\, with typical awards between GBP 2\,000 and GBP 5\,000\; 
 projects with a total budget exceeding GBP 30\,000 are not supported. ELIG
 IBILITY: individual fine artists and small organisations and galleries\, w
 ith projects taking place in the UK\; students and educational studies are
  excluded\; successful applicants must wait two years before reapplying. A
 PPLICATION: direct to the Trust per its apply page. DEADLINE: 18 October 2
 026.\n\nOrganisation: The Elephant Trust\nLocation: UK. Projects must take
  place in the UK\; priority to fine artists and small organisations and ga
 lleries.\nAward: Grants to visual artists of up to GBP 5\,000\; typical aw
 ards range GBP 2\,000 to GBP 5\,000. Projects with a total budget exceedin
 g GBP 30\,000 are not supported. No application fee.\nDuration: Project gr
 ant\, no fixed duration.\n\nMore: https://elephanttrust.org.uk/apply/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://elephanttrust.org.uk/apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:UK. Projects must take place in the UK\; priority to fine artists 
 and small organisations and galleries.
END:VEVENT
