DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Black Public Media: BPM Open Call 2026 (USD 20\,000 for n
 onfiction features)
DESCRIPTION:Black Public Media\, the US public-media organization funding s
 tories of the global Black experience\, invites nonfiction feature-length 
 projects (60+ minutes) in a range of formats\, styles and genres\, with ex
 perimental and hybrid approaches welcome as long as they are grounded in r
 eal people and events (confirmed 24 September 2026). Up to five projects e
 ach receive USD 20\,000 to finance pre-production\, production or early po
 st-production\, plus an invitation to pitch at PitchBLACK in June 2027\, w
 here one project receives an additional USD 150\,000 award. BPM's 2026 pri
 orities include anti-DEI efforts in higher education\, housing inequities\
 , and redistricting's impact on voting rights\, though all subjects are co
 nsidered. IMPORTANT: the applicant or a key member of the production team 
 must be a US citizen or green-card holder\, with at least three years of p
 rofessional producing/directing experience or a senior producer attached\;
  the applicant must hold artistic\, budgetary and editorial control and ow
 n the copyright\, and the funding is a licensing agreement for public medi
 a distribution rather than an unrestricted grant. No industrial\, promotio
 nal or student films. TO APPLY: submit the project description\, productio
 n team bios\, financials and a work sample via BPM's Submittable portal by
  1 October 2026\, 11:59 pm PT.\n\nOrganisation: Black Public Media\nLocati
 on: US. Applicant (or a key member of the production team) must be a US ci
 tizen or green-card holder\; nonfiction feature projects about the global 
 Black experience.\nAward: USD 20\,000 in production funding for up to five
  projects\, each also invited to pitch at PitchBLACK in June 2027\, where 
 one project receives an additional USD 150\,000 award. Structured as licen
 sing agreements for public media distribution. Free to apply.\nDuration: P
 rojects in pre-production\, production or early post-production\; PitchBLA
 CK pitch June 2027.\n\nMore: https://blackpublicmedia.org/for-media-makers
 /bpm-open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://blackpublicmedia.org/for-media-makers/bpm-open-call/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:US. Applicant (or a key member of the production team) must be a U
 S citizen or green-card holder\; nonfiction feature projects about the glo
 bal Black experience.
END:VEVENT
