DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: No Drama 2.0: USD 50\,000 horror short film initiative (M
 onkeypaw x Universal x American Cinematheque)
DESCRIPTION:No Drama 2.0 is a short-film development and production initiat
 ive from Jordan Peele's Monkeypaw Productions\, Universal Pictures and Ame
 rican Cinematheque\, seeking writer-directors with bold\, genre-centered s
 tories. This edition's theme\, 'Fear is universal. Monsters are personal'\
 , asks filmmakers to redefine horror across cultures\, generations and soc
 ieties\, exploring the monsters we carry within us\, interpreted broadly a
 s personal fears\, afflictions or internal struggles rather than literal c
 reatures. SUPPORT: up to three filmmakers each receive USD 50\,000 to prod
 uce their submitted short film as a proof of concept for a feature\, plus 
 mentorship from Monkeypaw\, Universal and American Cinematheque executives
 \, eligibility to screen at Beyond Fest 2027\, and first-look consideratio
 n from Universal and Monkeypaw. ELIGIBILITY: solo writer-directors (no tea
 ms) aged 21+ by 1 December 2026 with legal authorization to work in the Un
 ited States\, prior directing experience (short\, proof of concept\, music
  video\, web series\, TV episode or feature)\, full ownership of submitted
  material\, and availability to participate in person in Los Angeles. HOW 
 TO APPLY: via FilmFreeway with an original short script (max 10 pages)\, a
  feature treatment (max 5 pages)\, a lookbook (8-15 pages)\, a personal st
 atement or pitch video (max 6 minutes)\, a creative portfolio (minimum 2 s
 amples)\, a resume and a hand-signed release form. No application fee. DEA
 DLINE: 30 September 2026 at 11:59 PM PDT.\n\nOrganisation: Monkeypaw Produ
 ctions\, Universal Pictures and American Cinematheque\nLocation: United St
 ates\; winners must be able to participate in person in Los Angeles. Open 
 to writer-directors with legal authorization to work in the US.\nAward: Up
  to three filmmakers each receive USD 50\,000 to fund production of a shor
 t film / proof of concept\, plus mentorship from Monkeypaw\, Universal and
  American Cinematheque executives\, eligibility to screen at Beyond Fest 2
 027\, and first-look consideration from Universal Pictures and Monkeypaw. 
 No application fee.\n\nMore: https://www.americancinematheque.com/no-drama
 -2dot0/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.americancinematheque.com/no-drama-2dot0/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States\; winners must be able to participate in person in L
 os Angeles. Open to writer-directors with legal authorization to work in t
 he US.
END:VEVENT
