DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Frame Contemporary Art Finland: Mobility and Production G
 rants (October 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Frame Contemporary Art Finland distributes Ministry of Educatio
 n and Culture funds to promote Finnish contemporary art internationally. T
 he October 2026 round covers two grant types: MOBILITY GRANTS (EUR 250-5\,
 000) for international presentation of existing artworks and professional 
 networking\, such as art fair participation\; and PRODUCTION GRANTS (EUR 2
 \,500-8\,000) for a new commission or international co-production\, which 
 requires additional funding and a collaboration agreement. Trips and prese
 ntations must take place outside Finland\; events in Finland are not eligi
 ble. The field is mainly visual art with an emphasis on contemporary art. 
 ELIGIBILITY: natural persons (artists\, art experts\, working groups) and 
 registered organisations that are Finnish or Finland-based\; projects must
  promote Finnish or Finland-based artists or professionals or showcase Fin
 nish art\; expenses for international artists not living in Finland are ex
 cluded\, and only activity after the application period closes can be fund
 ed. Apply via Frame's online grant service in Finnish\, Swedish or English
 . The next round (February 2027) adds publication grants. DEADLINE: 31 Oct
 ober 2026\, 23:59.\n\nOrganisation: Frame Contemporary Art Finland\nLocati
 on: Finland (applicants)\; funded activity takes place outside Finland.\nA
 ward: Mobility grants EUR 250 to 5\,000\; production grants EUR 2\,500 to 
 8\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: Application window 1 to 31 October 
 2026\; funded activity 1 November 2026 to 31 October 2027\; decisions by 3
 0 November 2026.\n\nMore: https://frame-finland.fi/en/grants/how-to-apply/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://frame-finland.fi/en/grants/how-to-apply/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Finland (applicants)\; funded activity takes place outside Finland
 .
