BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nl-embassy-brussels-cultural-support-nov-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: Netherlands Embassy in Brussels: Open Call for Cultural P
 roject Support
DESCRIPTION:The Netherlands Embassy in Brussels runs several open calls per
  year subsidising Dutch-Belgian artistic and cultural projects in Belgium 
 that strengthen the Netherlands' cultural profile and promote cooperation 
 between the two countries. All artistic disciplines are eligible\, with a 
 focus on performing arts\, visual arts\, cultural heritage\, creative indu
 stries and digital culture\; the embassy welcomes innovative formats\, cro
 ss-border exchange\, and work on participation\, inclusion\, equal rights 
 and sustainability. The subsidy (max EUR 5\,000) only covers costs related
  to the Dutch participation in the project\, such as travel and accommodat
 ion for Dutch participants\, art transport\, production\, and communicatio
 n for the Dutch segment. Projects must take place in Belgium (unless virtu
 al collaborations) and be accessible to the public\; personal development 
 projects are not eligible. ELIGIBILITY: professional creators\, organisati
 ons\, institutions and legal entities in Belgium with a company registrati
 on number\; Dutch artists typically take part via a Belgian partner or org
 aniser. Apply via the embassy (netherlandsandyou.nl). DEADLINES: 3 Novembe
 r 2026\, then 18 March 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Embassy of the Kingdom of th
 e Netherlands in Brussels\nLocation: Belgium. Applicants must be professio
 nal creators\, organisations\, institutions or legal entities in Belgium w
 ith a company registration number\; the subsidy covers the Dutch side of D
 utch-Belgian projects.\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 per project.\nDuration: Ro
 lling open calls with multiple deadlines per year\; next deadlines 3 Novem
 ber 2026 and 18 March 2027.\n\nMore: https://dutchculture.nl/en/grant/nlem
 bassy-brussels-open-call-for-support?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://dutchculture.nl/en/grant/nlembassy-brussels-open-call-for-suppo
 rt?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Belgium. Applicants must be professional creators\, organisations\
 , institutions or legal entities in Belgium with a company registration nu
 mber\; the subsidy covers the Dutch side of Dutch-Belgian projects.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mensch-maschine-visit-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Fellowship 2027: Energy G
 hosts (E-WERK Luckenwalde / Akademie der Künste)
DESCRIPTION:The Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Program is an annual fellow
 ship offering four fully funded fellowships to artists from around the wor
 ld\, run by the JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Akademie der Künste (Berlin) with V
 ISIT\, the artist-in-residence programme of the E.ON Foundation\, E-WERK L
 uckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art (Warsaw). The
  2027 edition particularly encourages projects at the intersection of art\
 , energy and ecology exploring the theme ENERGY GHOSTS: the unseen dimensi
 ons of energy approached through mythology\, cosmology or speculative fict
 ion\, the invisible infrastructures\, histories and residues that haunt co
 ntemporary life\, and energy as an ecological\, political or spiritual for
 ce. Proposals are welcome from visual art\, performance\, film\, installat
 ion\, sound\, writing and new media. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 20\,000 per fellow 
 for artist fees and production costs of a new project (research and develo
 pment\, travel\, material and presentation costs)\; three fellows receive 
 studio space and accommodation at E-WERK Luckenwalde (a former power stati
 on about 40 minutes south of Berlin)\, one is accommodated by the Akademie
  der Künste in Berlin. The three-month residency runs roughly September t
 o November 2027 with on-site presence of at least 75% required\, a retreat
  at Ujazdowski Castle in Warsaw in September 2027\, events across the thre
 e venues\, and a closing symposium in October 2027 at the Akademie der Kü
 nste where fellows show work in progress alongside the 2026 cohort. JURY: 
 Nolan Oswald Dennis\; Chus Martinez (Institute Art Gender Nature\, TBA21)\
 ; Sarah Johanna Theurer (Fondation Beyeler)\; Anh-Linh Ngo (Akademie der K
 ünste)\; and Tiara Roxanne. APPLICATION: via the VISIT portal at visit-en
 ergy.com/bewerben. DEADLINE: 1 December 2026\, 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation:
  JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Akademie der Künste\, VISIT (E.ON Foundation)\, E-
 WERK Luckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art\nLocati
 on: E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademie de
 r Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CCA in
  Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.\nAward: Four fully funded fel
 lowships of EUR 20\,000 each\, intended for artist fees and production cos
 ts of a new project (research and development\, travel\, materials and pre
 sentation costs)\, plus studio space and accommodation for the three-month
  residency.\nDuration: Three months\, roughly September to November 2027 (
 the AdK notice gives mid-August to mid-November)\; fellows must live and w
 ork on site at least 75% of the time.\n\nMore: https://adk.de/news/2026/10
 /open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademi
 e der Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CC
 A in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:inciter-art-open-call-tending-to-the-hearth-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inciter Art (Fractured Atlas): quarterly open call for es
 says\, 'tending to the hearth' (USD 750 stipend)
DESCRIPTION:Inciter Art\, the Fractured Atlas blog\, runs themed quarterly 
 open calls for short essays by artists and arts workers\, and this season'
 s theme is 'tending to the hearth': generosity\, solidarity and collective
  investment in the invisible infrastructure behind creative work. Pitch an
  idea through the form\; selected writers are notified one week after the 
 deadline\, get four weeks to write a first draft\, then one round of edits
  with the final due a week later\, with the Fractured Atlas editorial spec
 ialist available for support. Published pieces run 750 to 900 words. Edito
 rs look for pitches grounded in your own experience as an artist or arts w
 orker that say something new or a familiar thing in a new way. AI may be u
 sed only in a supporting role for writing (research\, structure\, grammar)
  and AI-generated images are not accepted\; every pitch is read by a human
 . Writers keep all rights and copyright\; Fractured Atlas may use the fina
 l piece in promotion with credit. Everyone who submits hears back. ELIGIBI
 LITY: artists and arts workers\; payment requires a W-9\, so it is set up 
 for US taxpayers. Pitches outside the themed call are also accepted and re
 viewed on a rolling basis. DEADLINE: Monday 2 November 2026\, 11:59PM ET\;
  later submissions are reviewed on a rolling basis.\n\nOrganisation: Fract
 ured Atlas (Inciter Art)\nLocation: Remote (online publication)\; payment 
 via W-9\, so US-based writers in practice.\nAward: USD 750 stipend per sel
 ected writer\, paid by ACH deposit or check once the first draft is finish
 ed (a W-9 form is required). No submission fee.\nDuration: About six weeks
  after selection: four weeks for a first draft\, one week for the final dr
 aft.\n\nMore: https://fracturedatlas.notion.site/3cf23f9f3dc880bd91dbfbe1a
 70df620?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fracturedatlas.notion.site/3cf23f9f3dc880bd91dbfbe1a70df620?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote (online publication)\; payment via W-9\, so US-based writer
 s in practice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:art4mental-open-call-vr-artists-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:Deadline: ART4MENTAL open call for artists: VR content for mental-h
 ealth support (EUR 5\,000 sub-grants)
DESCRIPTION:ART4MENTAL is a Creative Europe project (partners in Ukraine\, 
 Poland\, Czechia\, Estonia\, Sweden and Austria) selecting 20 artists to c
 reate immersive VR content and scenarios used in art-therapy and mental-he
 alth support sessions across Ukraine and the EU. Selected artists get prof
 essional training in VR technology and trauma-informed design\, local boot
 camps\, a residency in Ukraine's Carpathian Mountains\, study visits to re
 habilitation centres\, ongoing collaboration with mental-health profession
 als\, and present their work at European exhibitions and conferences\, inc
 luding an international exhibition in Poland. ELIGIBILITY: the official pa
 ge says residents of EU countries and Ukraine with a proven artistic pract
 ice and full availability for all mandatory activities\; the On the Move l
 isting adds that at least 10 of the 20 places go to artists from Ukraine a
 nd at least one each to Czechia\, Estonia\, Sweden and Austria\, so applic
 ants from other EU countries are eligible but not prioritised. Two stages:
  online form with supporting documents\, then an online interview\; select
 ed artists announced January 2027. DEADLINE: 11 November 2026 per On the M
 ove (the official page only says November 2026\; no time zone stated).\n\n
 Organisation: ART4MENTAL (Creative Europe project)\nLocation: Hybrid: onli
 ne training plus a residency in the Carpathian Mountains\, Ukraine\, and a
 n exhibition in Poland.\nAward: Sub-grant of up to EUR 5\,000 per artist f
 or 20 selected artists (EUR 100\,000 pool)\, plus VR training\, mentorship
 \, a residency in the Ukrainian Carpathians and exhibition opportunities. 
 No application fee.\nDuration: Selection by January 2027\; residency and e
 xhibition dates not yet published.\n\nMore: https://www.art4mental.com/app
 lication?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.art4mental.com/application?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: online training plus a residency in the Carpathian Mountai
 ns\, Ukraine\, and an exhibition in Poland.
END:VEVENT
