UID:berlin-senate-wiederaufnahmefoerderung-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261203
SUMMARY:Deadline: Berlin Senate: Wiederaufnahmefoerderung 2027 (revival fun
 ding for Berlin performing arts productions\, up to EUR 30\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Berlin's Wiederaufnahmefoerderung funds revivals of existing in
 dependent-scene productions\, covering rehearsals and performances for sol
 o and group projects across all performing art forms: theatre\, dance\, pe
 rformance\, music theatre and music. WHO: professional artists and indepen
 dent groups based in Berlin (not enrolled students)\, and institutions wor
 king mainly with the Berlin independent scene. The original production mus
 t have been staged successfully in Berlin (music productions may have prem
 iered elsewhere) and must previously have received Berlin Senate funding\;
  work on the revival must not have started\, and the same revival cannot a
 lready be funded by another Berlin or Hauptstadtkulturfonds programme. Min
 imum performance targets apply: generally four performances for theatre an
 d dance\, two for music and music theatre. WHAT YOU GET: up to EUR 30\,000
  per project for the March to December 2027 period. APPLICATION: electroni
 cally via the Berlin service portal with all attachments\; read the curren
 t Infoblatt and use the sample financing plan. ACCESS (Performing Arts Pro
 gramm Berlin) offers help with the online application. DEADLINE: 2 Decembe
 r 2026 at 14:00.\n\nOrganisation: Berlin Senate Department for Culture and
  Social Cohesion\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany. For professional Berlin-base
 d artists and independent groups (the artist\, or the majority of a group'
 s members\, must live and work in Berlin) and institutions working mainly 
 with Berlin's independent scene.\nAward: Up to EUR 30\,000 per project. No
  application fee.\nDuration: Funding period March to December 2027\, one s
 election round for 2027\; decision expected February 2027.\n\nMore: https:
 //www.berlin.de/sen/kultur/foerderung/foerderprogramme/wiederaufnahmefoerd
 erung/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.berlin.de/sen/kultur/foerderung/foerderprogramme/wiederaufn
 ahmefoerderung/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany. For professional Berlin-based artists and indepe
 ndent groups (the artist\, or the majority of a group's members\, must liv
 e and work in Berlin) and institutions working mainly with Berlin's indepe
 ndent scene.
END:VEVENT
