DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261205
SUMMARY:Deadline: Palestine Film Fund (Autumn 2026 cycle): up to EUR 15\,00
 0 for Palestinian filmmakers
DESCRIPTION:The Palestine Film Fund\, set up by the Palestine Film Institut
 e in 2025 so that Palestinians can tell their own stories\, gives financia
 l and professional support to Palestinian filmmakers worldwide in two roun
 ds a year. This is the autumn round. WHAT IS FUNDED: short films up to 30 
 minutes at development\, production or post-production stage\, and medium 
 or feature-length films at development or post-production stage only\; fic
 tion\, documentary\, animation\, hybrid\, experimental and essay forms are
  eligible\, series are not. WHO: the director must be Palestinian\, living
  in Palestine or the diaspora\, with a recognised link to Palestine\, and 
 aged 18 or over\; a non-Palestinian producer may apply if the director is 
 Palestinian. Feature and medium-length applicants need at least one previo
 usly directed short. Only producers (or director-producers) may apply for 
 post-production. One project per director per cycle\, and not while holdin
 g an active PFF grant. WHAT YOU GET: up to EUR 3\,000 (short\, development
 )\, EUR 7\,000 (short\, production or post)\, EUR 5\,000 (feature\, develo
 pment) or EUR 15\,000 (feature\, post-production). APPLICATION: online for
 m in English or Arabic\; questions to fund@palestinefilminstitute.org. DEA
 DLINE: 4 December (the fund page gives no year\; read as 2026 from the rou
 nd schedule\; past rounds closed at 23:59 Palestine time).\n\nOrganisation
 : Palestine Film Institute\nLocation: For Palestinian directors living in 
 Palestine or the diaspora\; projects can be made anywhere. Applications in
  English or Arabic.\nAward: Short films (up to 30 min): up to EUR 3\,000 f
 or development or EUR 7\,000 for production or post-production. Medium and
  feature films: up to EUR 5\,000 for development or EUR 15\,000 for post-p
 roduction (production stage not eligible). No application fee.\nDuration: 
 Per project\; decisions 10 to 12 weeks after the deadline.\n\nMore: https:
 //www.palestinefilminstitute.org/en/palestine-film-fund?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
