UID:ssn-small-research-grants-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115742Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Surveillance Studies Network: Small Research Grants 2026-
 27 (up to GBP 1\,500)
DESCRIPTION:The Surveillance Studies Network\, the scholarly charity behind
  the journal Surveillance & Society\, funds small research activities in s
 urveillance studies\, including work on surveillance technologies\, data\,
  biometrics and AI-driven monitoring. Grants can cover costs such as trans
 cription\, participant payments\, travel\, equipment or conference fees. E
 LIGIBILITY AND PREFERENCES: SSN members\, or non-members doing surveillanc
 e-related research who join\; preference for early-career scholars (doctor
 al students or PhD holders within five years)\, working in an economically
  under-resourced region\, who have not previously received an SSN Small Re
 search Grant. Priority goes to scholars from UN-ranked LDCs\, but applican
 ts from all under-resourced regions are welcome. HOW TO APPLY: one PDF by 
 email with a roughly one-page single-spaced proposal (planned activities\,
  why they matter to your research\, why your region counts as under-resour
 ced\, how you meet the preferences\, timeline) and a budget of one page ma
 ximum\, subject line "SSN Small Grants Application"\; check the SSN site f
 or the current contact address. TIMELINE: deadline 1 December 2026\, resul
 ts January 2027\, funds spent by 5 January 2028\, post-award report due 1 
 April 2028\; awardees are encouraged to write a Research Note for the SSN 
 Blink blog.\n\nOrganisation: Surveillance Studies Network (SSN)\nLocation:
  Worldwide\, with preference for researchers based in economically under-r
 esourced regions (priority to UN-ranked Least Developed Countries). Applie
 d by email\; no travel required to apply.\nAward: Up to GBP 1\,500 per pro
 ject\, plus a two-year SSN membership. The 2025-26 round made two awards. 
 No application fee.\nDuration: Funds to be spent during the 2026-27 academ
 ic year\, by 5 January 2028.\n\nMore: https://surveillance-studies.net/hon
 ours/ssn-small-research-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://surveillance-studies.net/honours/ssn-small-research-grants/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide\, with preference for researchers based in economically 
 under-resourced regions (priority to UN-ranked Least Developed Countries).
  Applied by email\; no travel required to apply.
END:VEVENT
