SUMMARY:Deadline: NSF: Security\, Privacy\, and Trust in Cyberspace (SaTC 2
 .0)\, January 2027 target date
DESCRIPTION:NSF's SaTC 2.0 programme (solicitation NSF 25-515) funds resear
 ch and education on the security\, privacy and trustworthiness of digital 
 systems. Named topics include privacy-enhancing technologies\, attacks on 
 and trustworthiness of AI systems\, and 'human aspects' work using social\
 , behavioural and economic methods\, so policy-oriented and socio-technica
 l research on tech is in scope alongside technical work. ELIGIBILITY: US i
 nstitutions of higher education and US-based non-profit\, non-academic org
 anizations such as independent research labs and professional societies. E
 ach person may appear on at most 4 SaTC proposals in any 12-month period\;
  projects over USD 600\,000 need additional collaboration and participatio
 n plans. PROCESS: proposals via Research.gov or Grants.gov. Target date is
  the last Monday in January annually (25 January 2027\, 5 p.m. submitter's
  local time by NSF default)\; proposals are accepted anytime but may miss 
 that review panel.\n\nOrganisation: U.S. National Science Foundation (NSF)
 \nLocation: United States. US universities and colleges and US-based non-p
 rofit\, non-academic organizations only.\nAward: Research projects up to U
 SD 1\,200\,000 over up to 4 years\; education projects up to USD 500\,000 
 over up to 3 years\; seedling projects up to USD 300\,000 over up to 2 yea
 rs. About 75 awards (around 60 research\, 15 education)\, roughly USD 60\,
 000\,000 per year subject to available funds. No application fee.\nDuratio
 n: 2 to 4 years depending on project type\n\nMore: https://www.nsf.gov/fun
 ding/opportunities/satc-20-security-privacy-trust-cyberspace/nsf25-515/sol
 icitation?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.nsf.gov/funding/opportunities/satc-20-security-privacy-trus
 t-cyberspace/nsf25-515/solicitation?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States. US universities and colleges and US-based non-profi
 t\, non-academic organizations only.
END:VEVENT
